IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g8-nouns`
IMPORT `g8-art26-demand`
IMPORT `g8-art27-28-required-steps`
IMPORT `g8-art32-36-appeals`
IMPORT `g8-tests-fixtures`

-- g8-tests-art32-36: tests of Part 8 (Articles 32 to 36).  Expected values were decided from the text of the Law before the module was run.
-- Each of the paragraphs of Article 33 for the appellant it names and for a stranger, each decision on both of its outcomes, the Attorney General on any decision, the "both times" structure of 33(5)
-- on both readings (F8.18), who is excluded from it (F8.13), the closed list (F8.4) and the deregistration on the charity's own application (F8.16); the ground of appeal at the tribunal and at
-- the court (F8.5); every power of the Tribunal, the court, the Minister and the Commissioner; the time limit on both sides of its last day on every combination of F8.6 and F8.12; and 36(3) and 36(4).

§ `Tests of Part 8`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN applicant IS A BOOLEAN
      charity IS A BOOLEAN
      attorneyGeneral IS A BOOLEAN
      served IS A BOOLEAN
      interested IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Appellant under Article 33`
`T33 an appellant who is` applicant charity attorneyGeneral served interested MEANS
    `Appellant under Article 33` WITH
        `an applicant for registration` IS applicant
        `a registered charity` IS charity
        `the Attorney General` IS attorneyGeneral
        `a person served with the notice that contains the requirement` IS served
        `a person with an interest in the registered name of the applicant` IS interested

`T33 an applicant` MEANS `T33 an appellant who is` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`T33 a registered charity` MEANS `T33 an appellant who is` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`T33 the Attorney General` MEANS `T33 an appellant who is` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`T33 a person served with a notice` MEANS `T33 an appellant who is` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`T33 a stranger` MEANS `T33 an appellant who is` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`T33 a stranger with an interest in the name` MEANS `T33 an appellant who is` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`T33 a registered charity served with a notice` MEANS `T33 an appellant who is` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`T33 another registered charity with an interest in the name` MEANS `T33 an appellant who is` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`T33 another applicant with an interest in the name` MEANS `T33 an appellant who is` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

-- The right of appeal for an appellant, a decision (subject and outcome) and whether the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration; the charity test and the name are
-- not at issue (the charity test met at both times, no name undesirable).
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36`
      who IS AN `Appellant under Article 33`
      thing IS A `Subject of a decision of the Commissioner`
      result IS AN `Outcome of a decision of the Commissioner`
      own IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Right of appeal under Article 33`
`T33 the right of appeal` interp who thing result own MEANS
    `Art 33 the right of appeal` interp
        (`Appeal under Article 33` WITH
            appellant IS who
            `decision appealed` IS (`Decision of the Commissioner` WITH subject IS thing, outcome IS result)
            `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration` IS own)
        TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE

`T33 register` MEANS `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`
`T33 restricted section` MEANS `whether to enter a charity in the restricted section, Article 9(6) and (7)`
`T33 name permission` MEANS `whether to permit a change or addition of registered name, Article 12(4)`
`T33 name requirement` MEANS `whether to require a charity to apply to change its registered name, Article 12(6)`
`T33 purposes amendment` MEANS `whether to approve a proposed amendment of the charity's purposes, Article 13(3)`
`T33 statement amendment` MEANS `whether to approve a proposed amendment of the registered public benefit statement, Article 13(4)(b)`
`T33 deregister on application` MEANS `whether to deregister a charity on its own application, Article 15(3)`
`T33 deregister otherwise` MEANS `whether to deregister a charity in other cases, Article 16`
`T33 Article 26 requirement` MEANS `whether to impose a requirement contained in a notice under Article 26`
`T33 required steps requirement` MEANS `whether to impose a requirement contained in a required steps notice`
`T33 other matter` MEANS `any other matter`
`T33 does` MEANS `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
`T33 refuses` MEANS `the Commissioner refuses`

§§ `33(1) -- an applicant for registration`

#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 an applicant` `T33 register` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(1)(a)`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 an applicant` `T33 restricted section` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(1)(b)`
-- The applicant is registered: nothing to appeal under (1).
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 an applicant` `T33 register` `T33 does` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 an applicant` `T33 restricted section` `T33 does` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- Another applicant's refusal is not the appellant's own.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 an applicant` `T33 register` `T33 refuses` FALSE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- An applicant has no appeal against the other kinds of decision.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 an applicant` `T33 deregister otherwise` `T33 does` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 an applicant` `T33 other matter` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`

§§ `33(2) -- a registered charity: the five decisions, each on both outcomes`

#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 deregister otherwise` `T33 does` TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(a)`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 deregister otherwise` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 name permission` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(b)`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 name permission` `T33 does` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 name requirement` `T33 does` TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(c)`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 name requirement` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 purposes amendment` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(d)`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 purposes amendment` `T33 does` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 statement amendment` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(e)`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 statement amendment` `T33 does` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- A decision about another charity is not the appellant's own.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 deregister otherwise` `T33 does` FALSE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- A stranger has no appeal under (2).
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a stranger` `T33 deregister otherwise` `T33 does` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- T12: the list is closed.  A general-section charity's refused request for the restricted section (Article 9(7)), a refusal to deregister on application (Article 15(3)(b)), and any other decision:
-- no appeal is given by Part 8.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 restricted section` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 deregister on application` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 other matter` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 register` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- F8.4 other reading: by analogy, those two (and only those two) are appealable.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.4` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 restricted section` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal by analogy with Article 33(1)(b)`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.4` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 deregister on application` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal by analogy with Article 33(2)(a)`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.4` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 other matter` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.4` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 name permission` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(b)`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.4` `T33 a stranger` `T33 restricted section` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`

-- F8.16: a deregistration GRANTED on the charity's own application (Article 15(3)(a)).  Taken: within 33(2)(a).  Other reading: not.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 deregister on application` `T33 does` TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(a)`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.16` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 deregister on application` `T33 does` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.16` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 deregister otherwise` `T33 does` TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(a)`

§§ `33(3) -- a person served with a notice`

#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a person served with a notice` `T33 Article 26 requirement` `T33 does` FALSE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(3)`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a person served with a notice` `T33 required steps requirement` `T33 does` FALSE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(3)`
-- Not the person served.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a stranger` `T33 Article 26 requirement` `T33 does` FALSE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- A refusal to impose a requirement is not a decision the person served can appeal.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a person served with a notice` `T33 Article 26 requirement` `T33 refuses` FALSE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- Another kind of decision.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a person served with a notice` `T33 other matter` `T33 does` FALSE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- A registered charity served with an Article 26 notice has the right through 33(3), though 33(2) does not list the decision.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity served with a notice` `T33 Article 26 requirement` `T33 does` TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(3)`

§§ `33(4) -- the Attorney General`

#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 the Attorney General` `T33 other matter` `T33 refuses` FALSE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(4)`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 the Attorney General` `T33 restricted section` `T33 refuses` FALSE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(4)`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 the Attorney General` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(4)`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 the Attorney General` `T33 deregister on application` `T33 refuses` FALSE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(4)`

§§ `33(5) -- any other person, against a decision to register (F8.13, F8.18)`

-- The right of appeal of a stranger against the decision to register an applicant, for given facts at the two times: the charity test at the time of the application and of the appeal, and whether
-- the name was undesirable at each.
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36`
      who IS AN `Appellant under Article 33`
      thing IS A `Subject of a decision of the Commissioner`
      result IS AN `Outcome of a decision of the Commissioner`
      own IS A BOOLEAN
      metThen IS A BOOLEAN
      meetsNow IS A BOOLEAN
      badThen IS A BOOLEAN
      badNow IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Right of appeal under Article 33`
`T33 the right of appeal at the two times` interp who thing result own metThen meetsNow badThen badNow MEANS
    `Art 33 the right of appeal` interp
        (`Appeal under Article 33` WITH
            appellant IS who
            `decision appealed` IS (`Decision of the Commissioner` WITH subject IS thing, outcome IS result)
            `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration` IS own)
        metThen meetsNow badThen badNow

-- The charity test failed at both times: ground (a).  Name fine.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a stranger` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(a)`
-- Failed at the application only (it meets the test now): not at both times.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a stranger` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- Failed at the appeal only (it met the test then).
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a stranger` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- The charity test met at both times: no ground (a), and no interest in the name: nothing.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a stranger` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- Ground (b): an interested appellant, the name undesirable at both times.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a stranger with an interest in the name` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(b)`
-- ... not without the interest ...
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a stranger` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- ... not if the name was undesirable at one time only.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a stranger with an interest in the name` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a stranger with an interest in the name` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- Both grounds at both times: (a) is named first.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a stranger with an interest in the name` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(a)`
-- F8.18, the discriminating case: the charity test failed at the application but is met at the appeal; the name was fine at the application but undesirable at the appeal; the appellant has an interest.
-- Taken: each ground must hold at both times - neither does.  Other reading: some ground holds at each time - (a) at the application, (b) at the appeal.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a stranger with an interest in the name` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.18` `T33 a stranger with an interest in the name` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(5) on grounds that differ between the two times`
-- The readings agree where one ground holds at both times.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.18` `T33 a stranger` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(a)`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.18` `T33 a stranger with an interest in the name` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(b)`
-- On the other reading, an uninterested appellant cannot rely on (b): the name does not help it.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.18` `T33 a stranger` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- Only a decision to register is appealable by a stranger.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a stranger` `T33 register` `T33 refuses` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a stranger` `T33 restricted section` `T33 does` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- F8.13: another registered charity with an interest in a similar name, the name undesirable at both times.  Taken: excluded.  Other reading: it may appeal.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 another registered charity with an interest in the name` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.13` `T33 another registered charity with an interest in the name` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(b)`
-- ... and another applicant likewise.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 another applicant with an interest in the name` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.13` `T33 another applicant with an interest in the name` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(b)`
-- The applicant concerned (own application) is excluded on both readings; as is the charity it became.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.13` `T33 another applicant with an interest in the name` `T33 register` `T33 does` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.13` `T33 another registered charity with an interest in the name` `T33 register` `T33 does` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- The Attorney General is excluded from 33(5) and has 33(4).
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 the Attorney General` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(4)`

-- The yes/no question.
GIVEN who IS AN `Appellant under Article 33`
      thing IS A `Subject of a decision of the Commissioner`
      result IS AN `Outcome of a decision of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`T33 may appeal, favoured reading, own decision` who thing result MEANS
    `Art 33 the person may appeal the decision` `the favoured interpretation`
        (`Appeal under Article 33` WITH
            appellant IS who
            `decision appealed` IS (`Decision of the Commissioner` WITH subject IS thing, outcome IS result)
            `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration` IS TRUE)
        TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `T33 may appeal, favoured reading, own decision` `T33 an applicant` `T33 register` `T33 refuses`
#ASSERT `T33 may appeal, favoured reading, own decision` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 name permission` `T33 refuses`
#ASSERT `T33 may appeal, favoured reading, own decision` `T33 the Attorney General` `T33 other matter` `T33 does`
#ASSERT NOT `T33 may appeal, favoured reading, own decision` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 restricted section` `T33 refuses`
#ASSERT NOT `T33 may appeal, favoured reading, own decision` `T33 a stranger` `T33 register` `T33 refuses`

§§ `34(1) -- the ground of an appeal to the tribunal`

#ASSERT `Art 34(1) the appeal has a ground` (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `wrong`, `respect alleged` IS `its merits`)
#ASSERT `Art 34(1) the appeal has a ground` (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `wrong`, `respect alleged` IS `the facts`)
#ASSERT `Art 34(1) the appeal has a ground` (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `wrong`, `respect alleged` IS `the law`)
#ASSERT `Art 34(1) the appeal has a ground` (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `unreasonable`, `respect alleged` IS `its merits`)
#ASSERT `Art 34(1) the appeal has a ground` (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `unreasonable`, `respect alleged` IS `the facts`)
#ASSERT `Art 34(1) the appeal has a ground` (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `unreasonable`, `respect alleged` IS `the law`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 34(1) the appeal has a ground` (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `neither wrong nor unreasonable`, `respect alleged` IS `its merits`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 34(1) the appeal has a ground` (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `wrong`, `respect alleged` IS `some other respect`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 34(1) the appeal has a ground` (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `wrong`, `respect alleged` IS `all the circumstances of the case`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 34(1) the appeal has a ground` (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `neither wrong nor unreasonable`, `respect alleged` IS `some other respect`)

§§ `34(2) and 34(3) -- the powers of the tribunal`

-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 34(2)(a) the tribunal may make an interim order` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    -- no events

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 34(2)(a) the tribunal may make an interim order` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Charity Tribunal` DOES `make an interim order on an appeal or reference` AT 12

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 34(2)(a) the tribunal may make an interim order` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    -- no events

-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 34(2)(b) the tribunal may consider evidence` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    -- no events

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 34(2)(b) the tribunal may consider evidence` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Charity Tribunal` DOES `consider evidence put to the Commissioner or accept other evidence` AT 12

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 34(2)(b) the tribunal may consider evidence` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    -- no events

-- The two permissions together.
-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 34(2) the tribunal may make interim orders and consider evidence` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    -- no events

-- Using one leaves the other standing.
-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 34(2) the tribunal may make interim orders and consider evidence` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Charity Tribunal` DOES `make an interim order on an appeal or reference` AT 12

