§§ `35 -- appeal and reference to the court (F8.5)`

-- A party to the appeal to the tribunal, on the ground that the decision was unreasonable having regard to all the circumstances.
#ASSERT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `the favoured interpretation` TRUE FALSE (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `unreasonable`, `respect alleged` IS `all the circumstances of the case`)
#ASSERT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `the favoured interpretation` FALSE TRUE (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `unreasonable`, `respect alleged` IS `the facts`)
-- A stranger to the appeal, and not the Attorney General: no.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `the favoured interpretation` FALSE FALSE (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `unreasonable`, `respect alleged` IS `all the circumstances of the case`)
-- A party whose complaint is not unreasonableness.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `the favoured interpretation` TRUE FALSE (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `neither wrong nor unreasonable`, `respect alleged` IS `all the circumstances of the case`)
-- The discriminating case: a decision wrong in law but not unreasonable.  Taken: not a ground of an appeal to the court.  Other reading: it is.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `the favoured interpretation` TRUE FALSE (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `wrong`, `respect alleged` IS `the law`)
#ASSERT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.5` TRUE FALSE (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `wrong`, `respect alleged` IS `the law`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `the favoured interpretation` TRUE FALSE (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `wrong`, `respect alleged` IS `its merits`)
#ASSERT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.5` TRUE FALSE (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `wrong`, `respect alleged` IS `its merits`)
-- The readings agree on an unreasonableness complaint, and on a complaint that is neither.
#ASSERT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.5` TRUE FALSE (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `unreasonable`, `respect alleged` IS `all the circumstances of the case`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.5` TRUE FALSE (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `neither wrong nor unreasonable`, `respect alleged` IS `some other respect`)
-- Standing is still needed on the other reading.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.5` FALSE FALSE (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `wrong`, `respect alleged` IS `the law`)

